{"text": "David Nicholas Yonkovich\n\nHard working business management graduate with 6+ years of experience in accounting, analysis and solving problems seeking to\napply my abilities to support development of governmental policies and practices.\n\n+ Excellent at setting priorities + Motivated to learn new skills\n+ Professional and personable + Committed team player\n+ Strong analytical skills + Persistent problem solver\nEXPERIENCE The Heritage Foundation, Washington, DC January 2014 \u2014 Present\n\nStaff Accountant \u2014 Finance and Accounting Department\n\u00a2 Perform various day to day responsibilities to provide accurate financial\ninformation at the end of each month to all departments\n\u00a2 \u2014 Record all revenue and manage payable process for the organization\nand its related entities\ne Directly interact with research departments to facilitate corporate\nAMEX cards, individual department needs, and payments to vendors\neach week\n\u00a2 Maintain secure control over multiple credit card processing portals\n\u00a2 Continually improve upon current business practices throughout the\nyear to adapt to changing demands\n\u00a2 \u2014 Organize accounting information for end of year audit by outside\naccounting firm\n\u00a9 Uphold CFC certification and PCI compliance for the organization each\nyear\n\nConferenceDirect LLC, Los Angeles, CA July 2010 \u2014 Sept 2013\nProvided meeting and conference services via major hotel brands for large corporations\nand professional associations.\nRevenue Specialist May 2012 \u2014 September 2013\ne \u2014 Served as contact for company VIP sales associates\n\u00a2 Acted as liaison between hotel sales and company to resolve billing and\npayment differences\n\u00a2 Reconciled discrepancies and followed through with final payments\nBookings Administrator December 2011 \u2014 April 2012\n\u00a9 Verified sales entry of contracts with signed documents\n\u00a9 Met month-end deadlines and requirements for accurate data\n\u00abMade general ledger positing of appropriate revenue\nAccounts Payable Associate July 2010 \u2014 November 2011\n\u00a2 Responsible for daily commission payments to sales associates\n\u00a2 Required reconciliation and verification of multiple sources of detail\n\nProjects:\nv\u00a5 Managed British Petroleum account for services related to\nenvironmental clean-up\nY Participated in system conversion from QuickBooks to Microsoft\nDynamics Great Plains\nY Attended annual sales meetings in Washington DC and Orlando to\nprovide system training and other support as requested\n\nFirst American Corporation, Santa Ana, CA\nSummer Intern - Investor Relations Department Summer 2008\n\u00a2 Created profitability statements by region to support cost reduction initiative\n\u00a2 Performed analysis of title volumes by region to improve efficiency\ne \u2014 Analyzed office locations for ranking of lowest 20% with ultimate\ngoal of closure/relocation\nMailroom Clerk Summer 2005, 2006\ne Assisted in mail and package distribution for corporate campus\nsupporting over 2,000 employees",
